  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-10,-2]?$\n\n- ${-10,-9,-8,-4,-2}$\n- ${-9,-5,-4,-2}$\n- $-10<-6<-4<-3$",
  "worked_solution": "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<\u2026<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},\u2026,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is a partition of $[-10,-2].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$  since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-10.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of $[-10,-2]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
